This study investigates the long-term behavior of solutions to the Kardar-Parisi-Zhang type equation \begin{equation*}
\partial_t u = \Lambda(u,\lambda)(t,x) = \Delta u + \sum_{i=1}^m \lambda_i \partial_{x_i} u + \sum_{j=1}^n f_j(u,\lambda)(t,x) = 0.
\end{equation*} On a domain $(0,T) \times \Omega$ of $\mathbb{R}^d$ with $d=1$ and $\lambda \in \mathbb{R}^m \otimes \mathbb{R}^n$, where $\Omega$ is an open set, and shows the effect of parameter $\lambda$ on the presence or absence of solutions.
